{
	"name": "Challenger’s Call",
	"type": "feature",
	"img": "icons/magic/sonic/scream-wail-shout-teal.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>At 10th level, your @UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-class-features.Item.kdy4n7MRzAVYykI4]{Rise to the Challenge} ability improves. When you apply your offensive mark to a creature, you may force them to immediately make a Charisma saving throw against your combat maneuver DC. On a successful save, your offensive mark works normally.</p><p>On a failed save, your target is compelled to battle you. They have disadvantage on attack rolls against targets other than you and must make a Charisma save any time they willingly move more than 30ft away from you. On a failed save, they are unable to move any further. On a successful save, they become rattled but are able to move freely, while Rise to the Challenge is still active.</p><p>Creatures that are immune to fear effects are immune to your Challenger’s Call.</p>",
